      "type": "Dataset",
      "persistentId": "https://data.openei.org/submissions/57",
      "title": "NREL National Solar Radiation Database",
      "summary": "Satellite-derived half-hourly solar irradiance and meteorological data on a 4 km grid, covering the Americas and expanding regions.",
      "description": "The NSRDB provides GHI, DNI and DHI derived from geostationary satellite imagery through the PSM physical model, with supporting meteorology. It is the reference solar resource dataset for US work. The record is a good example of why access paths are modelled separately: the OEDI Parquet copy on S3 is anonymous and bulk-downloadable, while the developer API is key-gated and rate-limited, and the barrier classification differs between them even though the data is the same.",
